{"id": 35, "ts": 1780642529.8818138, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m still inclined to recommend **Candidate\u202fB**.\u202fBoth James and Sarah confirmed that we have no concrete observations on Candidate\u202fA\u2019s stress handling, decision\u2011making under pressure, crew\u2011cooperation, or professional communication, and we only know that A is unfriendly and eats unhealthily.\u202fWithout evidence on the very criteria that matter most for long\u2011distance flights\u2014reliability, calmness under pressure, and teamwork\u2014A cannot be judged as a safer choice than B.\u202fSimilarly, Candidate\u202fD also lacks any documented reliability incidents and is described as moody and a loner, raising concerns about crew interaction.\u202fIn contrast, B\u2019s record includes clear strengths: very conscientious (operational reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), and strong technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills).\u202fWhile his pretentiousness and occasional wrong tone are noted, these are manageable compared with the unknowns and concerns for A and D.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
